# Allow-list build context for deploy/docker/Dockerfile: only what the image build reads goes to the Docker daemon.
# Everything else (the .git folder, tests, docs, benchmarks, TestResults, local data, keys, certificates, .env files) stays out, so a secret
# in the working directory can never reach a layer or a remote builder.
*

!global.json
!Directory.Build.props
!Directory.Packages.props
!src/**

# Inside the allowed folders: no build output, no local settings, no key material, no data.
**/bin
**/obj
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/secrets.json
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.pfx
**/*.p12
**/keystore.json
**/namespaces.json
**/master.key
**/*.jsonl
**/*.log
